  m_text: 'ROI Name: Primary Motor Cortex (M1)


    Location: Located on the Precentral
    Gyrus


    Function: Controls voluntary movement of the opposite side of the
    body


    Clinical Relevance: Damage leads to the opposite hemiplegia (paralysis)
    (e.g. motor loss, muscle weakness) of the body

'
